real finding: Toxiproxy 'enabled:false' blocks NEW connections but doesn't kill Debezium's
already-established Kafka producer connection - the first order-dualwrite1 test still
succeeded because Debezium kept using its pre-existing connection through the disabled proxy
(a real Toxiproxy behavioral nuance, not a bug in our lab). Fixed by restarting Debezium so
its fresh reconnection attempt actually hits the disabled proxy.
